pokebw2-pointers.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): every cast of a pointer to u32 or s32 that clang
reports (-Wpointer-to-int-cast) as a uintptr_t or intptr_t cast: 192 sites, made by the column clang gives. Never worse
than before (a result stored in a u32 is cut as it was) and right wherever the address is computed on and cast back
(the heap alignments `(void *)(((u32)p + 0x1f) & ~0x1f)` in dwc_rapcommon.c crashed the boot). What still holds a
pointer in a u32 (about 130 casts from a u32 to a pointer, the maintainers' notes) needs its type changed, file by file.

